language 0.1.0
module deploy
  means
    Preparation of software artifacts for release and the placement of
    releases into environments intended for execution.

entity artifact : thing
  means
    artifact: an immutable result of a build, fit for storage, transfer or
    deployment.

entity build : thing
  means
    build: a reproducible process producing artifacts from definite source
    materials and settings.

entity release : thing
  means
    release: an identified coherent set of artifacts and information, approved
    for deployment.

entity deployment : thing
  means
    deployment: a single act of placing a definite release onto a definite
    target with a definite configuration.

entity target : thing
  means
    target: an addressable computing environment, or part of one, onto which a
    release may be placed.

entity environment : thing
  means
    environment: the deployment targets and infrastructure conditions in which
    a system runs.

entity configuration : thing
  means
    configuration: a set of values determining the behaviour of a deployed
    release without changing its artifacts.
